# Source tree. Committing any of it causes conflicts and bloats the repository.
Binaries/
DerivedDataCache/
Intermediate/
Saved/
Build/

# Visual Studio solution and project files: regenerate with
#   dotnet <engine>/Engine/Binaries/DotNET/UnrealBuildTool/UnrealBuildTool.dll \
#     -projectfiles -project=game/Cataclysm.uproject -game -rocket -progress
*.sln
*.slnx
.vsconfig
.vs/
.idea/
*.VC.db
*.opensdf
*.sdf
*.suo

# Built lighting and reflection data for a map, written next to the .umap as
# <MapName>_BuiltData.uasset. The engine regenerates it from a lighting build, so
# it is output rather than source. This project never bakes lighting: it renders
# with Lumen, and dungeon floors are generated at run time so they cannot be baked
# at all. tools/generate_input_assets.py makes every light in the sandbox level
# Movable for that reason, so nothing should produce one of these files. The rule
# is here in case something does, because these files go through Git LFS and each
# save stores another full copy. Issue #140 has the reasoning; the same rule is in
# GitHub's own UnrealEngine.gitignore template.
#
# If a map ever does need baked lighting, add an exception for that one map rather
# than deleting this line: !game/Content/Maps/L_Whatever_BuiltData.uasset
*_BuiltData.uasset

# Per-developer scratch space. Unreal creates a folder here per user and treats
# it as a sandbox rather than as project content, so nothing in it is shared.
game/Content/Developers/

# --- Third-party asset packs -------------------------------------------------
#
# Downloaded from Fab and left where Fab installs them, at the root of Content.
# They are 17.31 GB as of 2026-08-07 and every .uasset in them goes through Git
# LFS, so committing them would put 17 GB into LFS storage and draw on LFS
# bandwidth on every clone and every continuous integration checkout. A GitHub
# Free or Pro account includes 10 GiB of each per month
# (https://docs.github.com/en/billing/concepts/product-billing/git-lfs).
#
# They do not need to be in git. They are free, Epic still hosts them, and anyone
# can re-acquire them from their own Fab library. The durable record is
# game/docs/enemy-source-assets.md, which names which pack plays which enemy and
# carries every measurement taken from them. That file is text and IS committed.
#
# WORK DERIVED FROM THESE PACKS DOES NOT GO IN THESE FOLDERS. A retargeted
# animation or an animation Blueprint is this project's own work and belongs in
# git. Saved inside one of these folders it is dropped by `git add` with no error
# and no warning. It goes in game/Content/Enemies/<Cataclysm>/<Enemy>/ instead;
# game/docs/content-layout.md is the full convention.
#
# EVERY LINE IN THIS BLOCK IS PARSED. tools/third_party_content.py reads the
# patterns between the two markers below so that this file stays the single place
# the vendor list is written down. Add a new vendor's folder here and the tests
# that depend on it follow automatically. Keep one pattern per line.
#
# THIRD-PARTY-PACKS-BEGIN
game/Content/Paragon*/
game/Content/_SplineVFX/
game/Content/SplineEffect2/
game/Content/Vefects/
game/Content/Knife_light/
# THIRD-PARTY-PACKS-END

# Unreal crash and log output
*.log
Crashes/

# A directory called dev/null holding four Git LFS hook scripts (post-checkout,
# post-commit, post-merge, pre-push). Nothing in this project puts it there on
# purpose. It appears when a git command runs with core.hooksPath set to
# /dev/null: Git for Windows resolves that to a relative path, and Git LFS
# writes its hooks into it. Any command that runs the LFS filter over a tracked
# file reinstalls the hooks, so git clone, git checkout and git add all do it in
# this repository, because *.uasset and *.umap are LFS-tracked. Issue #195 has
# the reproduction. The leading slash anchors this to the repository root so a
# real dev/ directory somewhere below is still tracked.
/dev/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.claude/handoff.md

# The editor's own copy of the asset-viewer preview scene profiles. Running the
# interactive editor rewrites game/Config/DefaultEditor.ini with about 57
# kilobytes of `[/Script/AdvancedPreviewScene.SharedProfiles]`, written by
# `USharedProfiles`, which is declared `UCLASS(config = Editor, defaultconfig)`.
# `defaultconfig` is what sends it to the PROJECT's ini rather than the user's,
# so the engine owns the file and will keep rewriting it. Issue #414.
#
# Its only committed content was `bAllowMultiplePIEInstances=True`, and issue
# #427 established that line did nothing: the name appears nowhere in Unreal
# 5.8, and `UEditorEngine` is declared `config=Engine` so it would not read this
# file anyway. Nothing was lost by dropping it.
game/Config/DefaultEditor.ini
